            <ArticleTitle>Left-handedness and inheritance of bronchial asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>371-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A statistically significant difference in mean laterality quotients of 15 asthmatic and 106 nonasthmatic children showed a coexistence of left-handedness and asthma early in life. It is suggested that this phenomenon is not only a fetal event as the Geschwind-Galaburda hypothesis claims but it is mainly based on maternal line inheritance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
